{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An external push can stale an approval without making the PR appear in the digest's review count."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The digest incorrectly counts a PR as awaiting review while its requested changes are still being implemented."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Status can recommend review or report an unknown state after the factory has already recorded the PR as merged."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A closed PR with a historical blocked land is reported as blocked and accompanied by an unusable retry instruction."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"outage","trigger":"unusual","reason":"Harmless text with five nested encoding layers can block publication even with an empty private-string list."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unreadable privacy policy can hide confirmation and identifiers after a mutation succeeds, leaving the agent uncertain and risking duplicate work."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A short registered credential can cause ordinary response keys and values to be withheld, making tool results unusable."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unreadable privacy policy causes the status tool to omit its state and next-action fields."},{"id":"C9","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Sequential requests can add session-start latency, but the evidence does not establish a timeout or other runtime failure."},{"id":"C10","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A fresh approval is incorrectly counted as needing review when no PR snapshot has been saved."},{"id":"C11","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unknown run filter returns a structured 400 response, so the demonstrated issue is only an HTTP status inconsistency."},{"id":"C12","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"MCP approvals are persisted and reported as made by a human, producing an inaccurate audit trail."},{"id":"C13","consequence":"diag","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A very long input produces a long digest line, but no character limit or resulting runtime failure was established."},{"id":"C6b","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The status response omits the state and next action when the privacy policy is unreadable, duplicating C8."}]}